      "name": "Attacker compromised nearly 1000 Zyxel switches since August (CVE-2026-7273)",
      "description": "A Chinese-speaking threat actor has exploited a vulnerability (CVE-2026-7273) in unpatched ZyXEL GS1900 Smart Managed Switches and has exfiltrated sensitive data from 996 devices across 48 countries, GreyNoise reported on Monday. CVE-2026-7273 exploitation is part of an unfolding operation The Zyxel GS1900 Series is a line of Gigabit Ethernet switches aimed at small and mid-sized business \u2026 More \u2192 The post Attacker compromised nearly 1000 Zyxel switches since August (CVE-2026-7273) appeared first on Help Net Security .",
